  "worked_solution": "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n55%>50%,\n$$\n\nmore than half of Maya's orders were takeout.\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n0.8>0.5.\n$$\n\nSo, more than half of Priya's orders were takeout.\n\n- Statement III is false. We can compare $55%$ and $0.8$ by converting the decimal into a percent. \n\nTo do this, we multiply it by $100:$\n\n$$\n0.8\\times 100=80%\n$$\n\nSince  $55%<80%,$ Maya did not have a greater percentage of takeout orders compared to Priya.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
